      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel FAQ</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"faq-container\">\n    <header class=\"faq-header\">\n      <h1 class=\"faq-title\">Pixel FAQ</h1>\n      <p class=\"faq-subtitle\">Click a question to reveal the answer.</p>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"faq-controls\">\n      <button id=\"expand-all\" class=\"btn\" type=\"button\">Expand All</button>\n      <button id=\"collapse-all\" class=\"btn\" type=\"button\">Collapse All</button>\n    </div>\n\n    <ul class=\"faq-list\" id=\"faq-list\">\n      <li class=\"faq-item\">\n        <button class=\"faq-question\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"answer-1\" id=\"question-1\">\n          <span class=\"faq-question-text\">What is a pixel?</span>\n          <span class=\"faq-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">▼</span>\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"faq-answer\" id=\"answer-1\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"question-1\" hidden>\n          <p>A pixel is the smallest unit of a digital image or display, representing a single point of color.</p>\n        </div>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"faq-item\">\n        <button class=\"faq-question\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"answer-2\" id=\"question-2\">\n          <span class=\"faq-question-text\">Why pixel art?</span>\n          <span class=\"faq-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">▼</span>\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"faq-answer\" id=\"answer-2\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"question-2\" hidden>\n          <p>Pixel art is a form of digital art where images are created using individual pixels, often with a retro aesthetic.</p>\n        </div>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"faq-item\">\n        <button class=\"faq-question\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"answer-3\" id=\"question-3\">\n          <span class=\"faq-question-text\">How do I create pixel art?</span>\n          <span class=\"faq-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">▼</span>\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"faq-answer\" id=\"answer-3\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"question-3\" hidden>\n          <p>You can use dedicated software like Aseprite, or even simple tools like MS Paint, focusing on individual pixels.</p>\n        </div>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"faq-item\">\n        <button class=\"faq-question\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"answer-4\" id=\"question-4\">\n          <span class=\"faq-question-text\">What are common pixel art sizes?</span>\n          <span class=\"faq-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">▼</span>\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"faq-answer\" id=\"answer-4\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"question-4\" hidden>\n          <p>Common sizes include 16x16, 32x32, and 64x64 pixels, often scaled up for display.</p>\n        </div>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"faq-item\">\n        <button class=\"faq-question\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"answer-5\" id=\"question-5\">\n          <span class=\"faq-question-text\">Can I use pixel art for websites?</span>\n          <span class=\"faq-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">▼</span>\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"faq-answer\" id=\"answer-5\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"question-5\" hidden>\n          <p>Yes, pixel art can be used as decorative elements or icons on websites, often with CSS image-rendering: pixelated.</p>\n        </div>\n      </li>\n    </ul>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "styles.css",
      "content": "/* Reset and base */\n*, *::before, *::after {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\nbody {\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  background: #1a1a2e;\n  color: #e0e0e0;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  align-items: center;\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  padding: 16px;\n}\n\n/* Container */\n.faq-container {\n  background: #16213e;\n  border: 4px solid #0f3460;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 24px;\n  max-width: 640px;\n  width: 100%;\n  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 #0f3460;\n}\n\n/* Header */\n.faq-header {\n  text-align: center;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.faq-title {\n  font-size: 2rem;\n  color: #e94560;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 2px;\n  text-shadow: 2px 2px 0 #0f3460;\n}\n\n.faq-subtitle {\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  color: #a0a0b0;\n  margin-top: 8px;\n}\n\n/* Controls */\n.faq-controls {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n.btn {\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  padding: 10px 20px;\n  background: #0f3460;\n  color: #e0e0e0;\n  border: 3px solid #e94560;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background 0.1s, transform 0.1s;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n\n.btn:hover {\n  background: #1a4a7a;\n}\n\n.btn:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid #e94560;\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\n.btn:active {\n  transform: translate(2px, 2px);\n  background: #0a2540;\n}\n\n/* FAQ list */\n.faq-list {\n  list-style: none;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 12px;\n}\n\n.faq-item {\n  border: 3px solid #0f3460;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n/* Question button */\n.faq-question {\n  width: 100%;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  align-items: center;\n  padding: 16px;\n  background: #1a1a2e;\n  color: #e0e0e0;\n  border: none;\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1.125rem;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  text-align: left;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background 0.1s;\n}\n\n.faq-question:hover {\n  background: #22223e;\n}\n\n.faq-question:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid #e94560;\n  outline-offset: -3px;\n}\n\n.faq-question:active {\n  background: #0f0f1f;\n}\n\n/* Arrow */\n.faq-arrow {\n  display: inline-block;\n  transition: transform 0.2s ease;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  color: #e94560;\n}\n\n.faq-question[aria-expanded=\"true\"] .faq-arrow {\n  transform: rotate(180deg);\n}\n\n/* Answer */\n.faq-answer {\n  padding: 0 16px 16px 16px;\n  background: #16213e;\n  border-top: 3px solid #0f3460;\n  color: #c0c0d0;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n.faq-answer p {\n  margin-top: 12px;\n}\n\n/* Responsive */\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .faq-container {\n    padding: 16px;\n  }\n  .faq-title {\n    font-size: 1.5rem;\n  }\n  .faq-question {\n    font-size: 1rem;\n    padding: 12px;\n  }\n  .faq-controls {\n    flex-direction: column;\n  }\n  .btn {\n    width: 100%;\n  }\n}",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n  const faqList = document.getElementById('faq-list');\n  const questions = Array.from(faqList.querySelectorAll('.faq-question'));\n  const expandAllBtn = document.getElementById('expand-all');\n  const collapseAllBtn = document.getElementById('collapse-all');\n\n  // Toggle answer for a single question\n  function toggleAnswer(question) {\n    const isExpanded = question.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';\n    const answerId = question.getAttribute('aria-controls');\n    const answer = document.getElementById(answerId);\n\n    if (isExpanded) {\n      question.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\n      answer.hidden = true;\n    } else {\n      // Collapse all other open answers\n      questions.forEach(q => {\n        if (q !== question && q.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true') {\n          q.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\n          const otherAnswerId = q.getAttribute('aria-controls');\n          document.getElementById(otherAnswerId).hidden = true;\n        }\n      });\n      question.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');\n      answer.hidden = false;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Event listener for each question\n  questions.forEach(question => {\n    question.addEventListener('click', () => toggleAnswer(question));\n  });\n\n  // Expand all\n  expandAllBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {\n    questions.forEach(q => {\n      q.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');\n      const answerId = q.getAttribute('aria-controls');\n      document.getElementById(answerId).hidden = false;\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Collapse all\n  collapseAllBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {\n    questions.forEach(q => {\n      q.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\n      const answerId = q.getAttribute('aria-controls');\n      document.getElementById(answerId).hidden = true;\n    });\n  });\n});",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel FAQ Page\n\nA simple, accessible FAQ page with a pixel-art theme. Built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No external dependencies or network requests.\n\n## Features\n\n- 5 FAQ items with questions and answers.\n- Clicking a question expands its answer and collapses any other open one.\n- An arrow indicates the open state (rotates when open).\n- \"Expand All\" and \"Collapse All\" buttons.\n- Keyboard accessible: questions and buttons are focusable and can be activated with Enter/Space.\n- ARIA attributes for expandable sections.\n- Responsive layout down to 360px wide.\n- Cohesive color palette with hover, focus, and pressed states.\n\n## Usage\n\nOpen `index.html` in any modern browser. No server required.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` – structure and content.\n- `styles.css` – pixel-themed styles.\n- `script.js` – interactivity.\n\n## License\n\nMIT",
      "description": ""
    }
  ]
